-- title:
--   Frobenius re-basing of rigidifications, up to a central scalar
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $r$ and $\bar r$ are primes with $\bar r \neq r$, and $N$ is a nonzero natural number with $r \nmid N$ (`hrr`, `hrN`).
--
--   The coefficients are: a characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal{O}$ which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with an irreducible element $\pi$ (`hπ`), $\pi$-adically complete (`hcomplete`), whose residue ring $\mathcal{O}/\pi$ has exactly $r$ elements (`hres`) and for which $(r) = (\pi)$ as ideals of $\mathcal{O}$ (`hunr`); and a characteristic-zero field $K_0$ which is a fraction field of $\mathcal{O}$.
--
--   The unramified layer is a characteristic-zero domain $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ which is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, equipped with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, subject to: completeness for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`); maximality of that ideal (`hOnr_max`); every element of $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal{O}$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`); every monic polynomial over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`); and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod{\pi}$ for all $x$ (`hFr`).
--
--   The quaternionic data are rationals $a, b$ such that $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ is indefinite ($0 < a$ or $0 < b$) and, for each height-one prime $v$ of $\mathbb{Z}$, the completion at $v$ is a division algebra precisely when $v$ contains $r$ or $\bar r$ (`hB`); a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule $\Lambda$ which is an order maximal among orders (`hΛ`) and contains every rational integer (`hΛℤ`); and a map $\mathrm{coord} \colon \Lambda \to \mathbb{Z}_{p^2}(r) \times \mathbb{Z}_{p^2}(r)$ satisfying `IsOrderCoord` (`hcoord`): it is additive, sends $1$ to $(1,0)$, is multiplicative for the twisted rule $(\alpha,\beta)(\alpha',\beta') = (\alpha\alpha' + r\,\beta\,\varphi(\beta'),\ \alpha\beta' + \beta\,\varphi(\alpha'))$ with $\varphi$ the Witt-vector Frobenius, is injective, has dense image modulo every power of $r$, and matches reduced traces.
--
--   The reduction data at $r$ are: a fake elliptic curve $A_0$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi$ with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure; a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module $X_0$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi$ of height $4$ (`hX₀`); formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of dimension $2$ along the unit section of $A_0$; and the hypothesis `hA₀` that $\theta_0$ presents the formal group of $A_0$ as $X_0$ compatibly with $\mathrm{coord}$.
--
--   The moduli data are: a ring homomorphism $\iota \colon \mathbb{Z}_{p^2}(r) \to O^{\mathrm{nr}}$; a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module $\Phi$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/r$ which is special relative to the reduction of $\iota$ (`hΦ`) and of height $4$ (`hΦ4`); a moduli package $M$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ at $r$ which is a Zariski sheaf (`hM`); and a family $\eta$ assigning, to every ring $B$ with a homomorphism $\psi \colon O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$ and $r$ nilpotent in $B$, a map from rigidified $\Phi$-objects over $B$ to $M(B,\psi)$. The hypothesis `hη` has three clauses: over Noetherian $B$, two admissible rigidified objects have the same image under $\eta$ if and only if they are isomorphic; $\eta$ commutes with base change along ring homomorphisms compatible with the legs, on admissible objects; and every point of $M(B,\psi)$ is, after passing to a finite family of localisations whose associated elements generate the unit ideal, the image under $\eta$ of an admissible rigidified object. Further, $E_0$ is a ring homomorphism from the centraliser of $\{\Phi.\mathrm{actEnd}\} \cup \{\Phi.\mathrm{varpiEnd}\}$ to $M_2(K_0)$, and `hE₀` asserts that $E_0$ is injective and that for some $m$ every matrix $A$ over $\mathcal{O}$ occurs as $r^{m} A$ in the image of $E_0$ while $r^{m} E_0(e)$ is always integral.
--
--   The comparison data are: a ring homomorphism $\kappa \colon O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi \to O^{\mathrm{nr}}/r$ compatible with the two quotient maps (`hκ`); a natural number $n_0$; and a $2$-tuple of power series $\beta_0$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/r$ which is an isogeny of height $4 n_0$ from $\Phi$ to the base change of $X_0$ along $\kappa$ (`hβ₀`).
--
--   Finally, $\Xi$ assigns, to every Noetherian $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $B$, every $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $\psi \colon O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent in $B$, and every pair consisting of a fake elliptic curve over $B$ together with a rigidification relative to $\psi$, a $G$-point of $M$ over $\mathcal{O}$, that is, a triple (leg $O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$, nilpotence of $r$, point of $M$ at that leg). Four hypotheses constrain $\Xi$: `hΞleg`, that over a $B$ all of whose idempotents are $0$ or $1$ the leg of $\Xi$ is $\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{k}$ for some $k \in \mathbb{Z}$; `hΞnat`, that $\Xi$ commutes with base change along an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $\varphi \colon B \to B'$ whenever the curve and the rigidification over $B'$ are pullbacks of those over $B$ along $\varphi$; `hΞiso`, that $\Xi$ takes equal values on two rigidified curves over the same $(B,\psi)$ whose underlying curves are isomorphic over $B$ compatibly with group law, $\Lambda$-action and level structure, provided in addition there are a morphism $ib$ of the reductions, a pullback morphism $uA$ of the auxiliary curves, and exponents $i_1, j_1$ for which $ib$ followed by the isogeny of the second rigidification, by $uA$ and by multiplication by $r^{i_1}$ equals the isogeny of the first rigidification followed by multiplication by $r^{j_1}$; and `hΞdef`, that over a connected Noetherian $B$ in which both $\pi$ and $r$ are nilpotent, given a formal module structure $(X,\theta)$ on the curve, there exist $j \le 1$ and a rigidified $\Phi$-object $t$ over $B$ with $t.X = X$, with $t$ a rigid transport of $(\theta_0, \kappa, \beta_0)$ through the rigidification at level $j$, with $t$ admissible for $\iota$ and the twisted leg $\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-j}$, and with $\Xi$ of the rigidified curve equal to the $G$-point with leg $\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-j}$ and point $\eta(t)$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses, the following holds for every Noetherian $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $B$, every $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $\psi \colon O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent in $B$, every $B$ all of whose idempotents are $0$ or $1$, every fake elliptic curve $E$ over $B$ with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure, and every rigidification $\rho$ of $E$ relative to $\psi$.
--
--   First, there exist a rigidification $\rho^{+}$ of the same curve $E$ relative to the twisted leg $\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}$ and an integer $c$ such that two conditions hold. (i) The $G$-points $\Xi(E,\rho)$ at the leg $\psi$ and $\Xi(E,\rho^{+})$ at the leg $\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}$ are related by the action of the $c$-th power of the central scalar $r \in K_0^{\times}$, viewed as a unit of $M_2(K_0)$: explicitly, there are an element $e$ of the centraliser of $\{\Phi.\mathrm{actEnd}\} \cup \{\Phi.\mathrm{varpiEnd}\}$ and natural numbers $k$, $m'$ with $E_0(e) = r^{k} \cdot g^{-1}$ for $g$ that central scalar power, with the power series attached to $e$ having kernel of degree $r^{2m'}$, and with the predicate `IsTranslate` for $\iota$, $\Phi$, $\eta$, $\mathrm{Fr}$ holding for that series, $k$, $m'$ and the two $G$-points. (ii) Level compatibility away from $r$: for every prime $\ell \ne r$ whose image in $B$ is a unit, every extra level structure at $\ell$ on $A_0$ (the binder for it re-uses the name `K₀`, shadowing the fraction field inside this clause) and every pair $C, C'$ of extra level structures at $\ell$ on $E$, if $C$ is carried into the chosen level structure of $A_0$ by $\rho$ — meaning that for every scheme $T$, every morphism $T \to \operatorname{Spec}(B/\pi)$ and every $T$-point $R$ of the reduced curve of $\rho$ over it, whenever $R$ followed by $\rho.g_b$ factors through the level scheme of $C$ then $R$ followed by the isogeny of $\rho$ and then by $\rho.g_A$ factors through the level scheme of $A_0$ — and if $C'$ is carried into it by $\rho^{+}$ in the same sense, then for every scheme $T$, every morphism $t \colon T \to \operatorname{Spec} B$ and every $T$-point $R$ of $E$ over $t$, $R$ factors through the level scheme of $C$ if and only if it factors through that of $C'$.
--
--   Second, the same assertion holds with $\mathrm{Fr}$ replaced by $\mathrm{Fr}^{-1}$: there exist a rigidification $\rho^{-}$ of $E$ relative to the leg $\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-1}$ and an integer $c$ such that $\Xi(E,\rho)$ and $\Xi(E,\rho^{-})$ are related by the action of the $c$-th power of the central scalar $r$ in the sense just described, and such that the level-compatibility clause holds with $\rho^{+}$ replaced by $\rho^{-}$.
--
--   This is the Frobenius re-basing step in the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison between the supersingular locus of a quaternionic moduli problem and Drinfeld's moduli of special formal modules: changing the unramified leg of a rigidification by $\mathrm{Fr}^{\pm 1}$ alters the associated point of the Drinfeld moduli package only by a central scalar $r^{c}$, and the re-based rigidification transports prime-to-$r$ level structures exactly as the original one does. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.exists_rigidification_frobTwist_zpow_isActBy_scalar_extraLevel_of_rigidifiedToG`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.exists_rigidification_frobTwist_zpow_isActBy_scalar_extraLevel_of_rigidifiedToG), where the twist is iterated to arbitrary integral powers of Frobenius, the level clause being needed by the fine-level consumers.
